WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.047
Five of the six criteria
roll up into two axes:

2
00:00:03.047 --> 00:00:08.475
how much the mission needs the application,
and how healthy it is to run and change.

3
00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:12.512
Dependencies stay out of both axes
and set the order of the moves.

4
00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:14.937
The grid shows where each corner points.

5
00:00:14.937 --> 00:00:15.901
Low value?

6
00:00:15.901 --> 00:00:17.275
Retire it first.

7
00:00:17.275 --> 00:00:18.950
High value and healthy?

8
00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:20.425
Keep it, on purpose.

9
00:00:20.425 --> 00:00:22.325
High value and unhealthy?

10
00:00:22.325 --> 00:00:26.200
Fix the platform or the code,
whichever is the real problem.

11
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:30.244
Every score also carries a flag
for how far you can trust it:

12
00:00:30.244 --> 00:00:32.350
measured, attested or assumed.

13
00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:35.013
Mostly assumed means no decision yet.

14
00:00:35.013 --> 00:00:39.901
And always prefer what's measured, like
usage logs, over what people believe.

15
00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:41.520
Next, the rules.
